                <pb facs="0382" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v03/pg352"/>

                <head>80. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On December 3, 1959, the President approved revisions in paragraph 60 of NSC
                    5906/1, which had been concurred in by the National Security Council and other
                    interested agencies in NSC Action No. 2155 that same day. (Memoranda from Lay to
                    the NSC, October 29 and December 3; both in Department of State, S/P–NSC Files:
                    Lot 62 D 1) Paragraph 60 concerned stockpiling policy. The general purpose of
                    the revisions, which reflected decisions taken at a Cabinet meeting on September
                    11, was to improve management of commodities in the stockpile and encourage
                    timely disposal of excess quantities. (Cabinet Paper CP–59–78/2, “Policies With
                    Respect to Stockpiling,” September 10, and minutes by L. Arthur Minnich of
                    Cabinet meeting on September 11; both <pb facs="0383" n="353" xml:id="pg353"/>
                    in Eisenhower Library, Whitman File, Cabinet Series) The four documents are in
                    the Supplement. For NSC 5906/1, see <ref target="#d70">Document 70</ref>.</p>
            </div>
